cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LMhdX in published work, cite the software and the benchmark sources used by your case."
title: "LMhdX: JAX-native inductionless liquid-metal magnetohydrodynamics"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jorge
    given-names: Rogerio
version: 1.4.0
date-released: 2026-09-15
repository-code: "https://github.com/uwplasma/LMhdX"
url: "https://lmx.readthedocs.io/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - magnetohydrodynamics
  - liquid metal
  - JAX
  - differentiable simulation
  - fusion engineering
abstract: >-
  LMhdX solves incompressible, inductionless liquid-metal MHD in fully developed
  duct cross-sections, periodic quasi-two-dimensional flow, and three-dimensional
  extruded ducts and pipes with spatially varying imposed magnetic fields. It
  provides JAX execution, analytical and manufactured verification, and
  reproducible FreeMHD comparison.
